{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Axon API",
    "description": "Read API for a personal Matrix state layer. Account-scoped resources nest under /v1/accounts/{account_id}; /v1/rooms is the cross-account aggregate.",
    "license": {
      "name": "AGPL-3.0-only",
      "identifier": "AGPL-3.0-only"
    },
    "version": "0.1.0"
  },
  "paths": {
    "/v1/accounts": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "accounts"
        ],
        "summary": "List the accounts this Axon manages, oldest first — the **client-visible**\nset: `active` and `deactivated`.",
        "description": "Logged-out (`deactivated`) accounts are included so a client that has lost the\n`account_id` can still discover one to offer re-login (the login verb both\nproduces and reactivates them). The transient `deleting` teardown state is\nexcluded — a row mid-removal isn't something to act on — but any account, in\nany state, can still be read by id via [`get_account`].",
        "operationId": "list_accounts",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Client-visible accounts (active + deactivated), oldest first",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ApiResponse_Vec_AccountDto"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/accounts/login": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "accounts"
        ],
        "summary": "Add or reactivate a Matrix account at runtime, then return the resulting\nactive account. Idempotent by `(homeserver_url, username)`: a new identity is\nminted, a logged-out (`deactivated`) account is reactivated, and an\nalready-`active` account is returned **unchanged** (a no-op — the desired end\nstate already holds, so the password isn't consulted and nothing is touched).\nAn account mid-deletion (`deleting`) is a `409`. `username` must be a full\nMatrix user ID (a malformed one is a `400`); bad credentials are a `401`. The\npassword is used once and never stored.",
        "description": "`homeserver_url` is optional: when omitted, the server discovers the\ncanonical homeserver from the user ID's server name (`.well-known/matrix/client`,\nfalling back to the server name itself) — so clients need only username +\npassword, and one canonical URL keys the identity no matter who logs it in.\nA failed discovery is a `502`. The `username` domain is then checked against\nthe homeserver's own declared server name (best-effort): a user ID written\nwith the homeserver's hostname (`@adam:matrix.example.org`) is a `400` whose\nmessage suggests the ID they almost certainly meant (`@adam:example.org`),\nrather than a misleading `401` — and never a silent login as a different\nidentity.\n\nSecret-bearing, so this route is loopback-only until the auth layer lands (see\nthe `route_layer` in [`router`](crate::router)).",
        "operationId": "login",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/LoginRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The active account (newly logged in, reactivated, or already active)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ApiResponse_AccountDto"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Malformed request (e.g. invalid user ID, or a user ID written with the homeserver's hostname — the message suggests the canonical spelling)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Credentials rejected by the homeserver",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "The account is being deleted",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "502": {
            "description": "Upstream homeserver error (including failed homeserver discovery)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/accounts/{account_id}": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "accounts"
        ],
        "summary": "Read a single account by id, in whatever lifecycle state it is — unlike the\nlist, a direct by-id read is not filtered to `active` (so a client can poll\nan account it knows and watch it transition). An unknown id is a 404.",
        "operationId": "get_account",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "account_id",
            "in": "path",
            "description": "Axon account id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "uuid"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The account",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ApiResponse_AccountDto"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No such account",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/accounts/{account_id}/events/{event_id}": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "events"
        ],
        "summary": "Read a single event by `(account_id, event_id)`. Redacted events come back\nmasked (`content`/`body` null, `redacted` true); an unknown id is a 404.",
        "operationId": "get_event",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "account_id",
            "in": "path",
            "description": "Axon account id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "uuid"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "event_id",
            "in": "path",
            "description": "Matrix event id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The event",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ApiResponse_EventDto"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No such event",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/accounts/{account_id}/logout": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "accounts"
        ],
        "summary": "Log a Matrix account out, then return the resulting (now `deactivated`)\naccount. Stops syncing it, invalidates its device token upstream (best-effort\n— an unreachable homeserver never fails the logout), and moves it to a\nlogged-out state, **retaining all of its data** (archive, search, media) so a\nlater login reactivates the same `account_id`. Idempotent: logging out an\nalready-logged-out account is a `200` no-op. An account mid-deletion\n(`deleting`) is a `409`; an unknown id is a `404`.",
        "description": "Secret-bearing / destructive, so this route is loopback-only until the auth\nlayer lands (see the `route_layer` in [`router`](crate::router)).",
        "operationId": "logout",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "account_id",
            "in": "path",
            "description": "Axon account id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "uuid"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The logged-out (deactivated) account",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ApiResponse_AccountDto"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No such account",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "The account is being deleted",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
